From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:24:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 135/151] Find: matches across line breaks when the pattern can
 match one

A regex query that can match a line break (". matches newline" on, an
inline (?s) flag, or an explicit \n, \r or \s) is now searched in the
lines joined instead of line by line: Find next and previous, Replace,
Replace all, the match count and the match highlights. Other queries
keep the per-line fast path.

Lines are joined with \n for every line ending, so foo\nbar matches in
LF, CRLF and CR files alike; a query naming \r gets each line's real
ending. Line breaks in the replacement take the file's own ending.
Replace all in this mode is one undo step. The count copies the text
only after the typing pause; highlights join the visible lines plus
200 lines around them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

